figure is 11.4 per cent that of Asia (Oyelaran-Oyeyinka and Abejirin, 2024).\n\nWhile African economies were moving at a slow pace, the population was growing rapidly. The annual average rate of population growth in the last 30 years is 2.6 percent. This is higher than the global average of 1.5 percent. Between 1980 and 2015, the continent’s population grew by 708 million, leaving the current total at 1,546,090,113. This represents 18.83 percent of total world population.\n\n12--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAsia GDP 2025 - StatisticsTimes.com (https://www.statisticstimes.com/economy/asia-gdp.php)\nciteturn51search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.7 years ago; Crawled: today; Subregion  | GDP (billions of $)  | Share (%) in Asia  | Share (%) in World ... 1970  | 2000  | 2023  | 1970  | 2000  | 2023  | 1970  | 2000  | 2023 ... 1994  | 8,234.425  | 9,491.572  | 29.17\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNominal GDP (US dollars) - East Asia and Pacific - World Bank - Yearly - FetchSeries Time Series Download (https://www.fetchseries.com/global-gdp-data/nominal-gdp-in-us-dollars-world-bank/nominal-gdp-us-dollars-east-asia-and-pacific-world-bank-yearly)\nciteturn51search4 [wordlim: 200] # Nominal GDP (US dollars) - East Asia and Pacific - World Bank - Yearly ... Dec 31, 1990  | 4,870,448,081,100.07 ... Dec 31, 2024  | 32,200,466,782,431.1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe ACT’s private equity takeover and the future of testing (https://www.insidehighered.com/news/admissions/traditional-age/2024/04/25/acts-private-equity-takeover-and-future-testing)\nciteturn51search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.5 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; April 25, 2024 ... After its acquisition by Nexus Capital, ACT will transition from a nonprofit organization into a for-profit company.\n--------------------------------------------------------